From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:47:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: t8132-platform-data: resolve the CIO PMGR
 block

Since the ACIO3 USB4 host router description added pmgr_cio
(power-management@380780000, an apple,t8132-pmgr with only a reset
controller and no power states), the platform hand-off's policy pass
could not resolve it in the built-in policy, logged "cannot resolve
PMGR policy for /soc/power-management@380780000: -1" on every boot, and
discarded its whole changeset: no PMGR policy, no supplied platform
nodes, no boot-framebuffer domain pass.

Add the block to the policy data with no power states, as the SoC-tree
reference needs resolving but describes no domain. Matches the node the
Aurora integration tree already carries for it.

Fixes: 91e61e25fbcb ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Describe the ACIO3 USB4 host router")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
index 309733a8d2..c5f48ecb6e 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
@@ -17,6 +17,13 @@ pmgr: power-management@380700000 {
 			reg = <0x3 0x80700000 0 0x14000>;
 		};
 
+		/* Describes no domain; resolves the CIO PMGR the SoC tree carries. */
+		pmgr_cio: power-management@380780000 {
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+			reg = <0x3 0x80780000 0 0x4000>;
+		};
+
 		pmgr_mini: power-management@388280000 {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
-- 
2.43.0

